WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:10.360
That's loud, that's gladdening, and it's awesome.

00:10.360 --> 00:16.020
You know, it's gladdening to come in.

00:16.020 --> 00:17.020
How are you, Alison?

00:17.020 --> 00:18.020
Good, Jesse.

00:18.020 --> 00:19.020
Cell phone yet?

00:19.020 --> 00:20.020
No, but I hope to get to you soon.

00:20.020 --> 00:21.020
I want to feed them and get them out before Joe gets here.

00:21.020 --> 00:22.020
Oh, is Joe seeing you again tonight?

00:22.020 --> 00:23.020
Sure.

00:23.020 --> 00:26.020
Remember I read you the note he sent over this morning.

00:26.020 --> 00:29.020
He said that we go to a few places first in the afternoon

00:29.020 --> 00:33.520
And then if I couldn't find a ring I wanted for Ralph, he'd come back tonight with more samples.

00:33.520 --> 00:37.020
You sure got in a lot of trouble to get Ralph a Christmas gift.

00:37.020 --> 00:40.020
Trixie's been a good husband, and I want to make sure he'll be happy.

00:40.020 --> 00:45.020
Well, I gotta get back upstairs and cook dinner for my good husband.

00:48.020 --> 00:49.020
I gotta hurry up.

00:49.020 --> 00:50.020
Go on.

00:50.020 --> 00:51.520
Oh, I almost forgot.

00:51.520 --> 00:54.020
I came down to return the cup of sugar you let me have yesterday.

00:54.020 --> 00:59.020
Oh, thanks, Trixie.

00:59.020 --> 01:05.020
Once again, it's been a long, long time.

01:05.020 --> 01:11.020
Kiss me once, kiss me twice, kiss me once again.

01:16.020 --> 01:17.020
Alex!

01:17.020 --> 01:18.020
Alex!

01:18.020 --> 01:19.020
Thank you, Ralph.

01:19.020 --> 01:20.020
Yeah, come on.

01:20.020 --> 01:21.020
I'll be right out.

01:21.020 --> 01:24.020
Well, hurry up will ya, I'm starving.

01:24.020 --> 01:25.520
I lost some of the bones.

01:25.520 --> 01:28.020
Oh, yeah.

01:28.020 --> 01:29.020
Here.

01:29.020 --> 01:32.020
I'll start standing in a half hour, we'll leave together.

01:32.020 --> 01:34.020
And listen, we're bowling the same team tonight.

01:34.020 --> 01:35.020
Don't worry about it.

01:35.020 --> 01:36.020
They haven't got a chance.

01:36.020 --> 01:37.520
They haven't got a...

01:37.520 --> 01:39.520
They haven't got a what?

01:39.520 --> 01:42.020
Hey, hey, hey, what's the matter?

01:45.520 --> 01:46.020
Look out.

01:46.020 --> 01:52.020
What's the matter, Ralph?

01:52.020 --> 01:55.020
Get a load of this.

01:55.020 --> 02:03.020
Dear Alex, meet me at the same spot this afternoon and I'll take you around to a few places.

02:03.020 --> 02:09.020
Then I'll sneak up to your place tonight while Ralph is out bowling.

02:09.020 --> 02:11.020
Signed, Joe.

02:11.020 --> 02:12.020
Yes.

02:12.020 --> 02:13.020
Get a load of that.

02:13.020 --> 02:17.020
Then I'll sneak up to your place tonight while Ralph is out bowling.

02:17.020 --> 02:26.020
This bum is stealing my wife, sneaking up to my apartment, and he's got the gall to call me by my first name.

02:26.020 --> 02:28.020
How about that?

02:28.020 --> 02:30.020
Oh, that's terrible.

02:30.020 --> 02:31.020
Terrible?

02:31.020 --> 02:32.020
It's worse than that.

02:32.020 --> 02:36.020
This guy's trying to destroy an empire that's taken me 12 years to build.

02:36.020 --> 02:38.020
Hey, listen, Ralph.

02:38.020 --> 02:40.020
Listen, listen, maybe it isn't Alex's fault.

02:40.020 --> 02:44.020
I had the same thing happen to a friend of mine. It wasn't a friend's wife's fault.

02:44.020 --> 02:47.020
He was minding her own business, drinking all alone in a bar.

02:47.020 --> 02:52.020
Some guy come along and picked her up.

02:52.020 --> 02:55.020
What am I gonna do? What am I gonna do?

02:55.020 --> 03:00.020
Listen, why don't you slap her around a little so she realizes what a sweet guy you are.

03:00.020 --> 03:02.020
I can't do anything like that.

03:02.020 --> 03:04.020
What are you gonna do?

03:04.020 --> 03:06.020
I don't know yet.

03:06.020 --> 03:08.020
I'll do something, though.

03:08.020 --> 03:09.020
I'll do something.

03:09.020 --> 03:11.020
Ralph, don't let it upset you, will you, pal?

03:11.020 --> 03:13.020
Don't let it upset you.

03:13.020 --> 03:17.020
You're bull rockin' tonight.

03:17.020 --> 03:20.020
You don't think for a minute that I'd step out of here tonight, don't you?

03:20.020 --> 03:21.020
With that snake coming up here?

03:21.020 --> 03:23.020
No, sir, I ain't scared.

03:23.020 --> 03:24.020
Ralph.

03:24.020 --> 03:25.020
Hi, Ralph.

03:25.020 --> 03:26.020
I gotta go up.

03:26.020 --> 03:27.020
Hey.

03:27.020 --> 03:28.020
Hi, Eddie.

03:28.020 --> 03:32.020
Hello, Alex.

03:32.020 --> 03:33.020
Hey, Alex.

03:33.020 --> 03:34.020
Yeah?

03:34.020 --> 03:37.020
My wife doesn't go out with you in the afternoons.

03:37.020 --> 03:40.020
Come on, then.

03:40.020 --> 03:49.020
Oh, please, sir.

03:49.020 --> 03:51.020
What's the matter with him?

03:51.020 --> 03:55.020
Don't stand there, Ralph. Hurry up and eat.

03:55.020 --> 03:58.020
What do you mean, hurry up and eat?

03:58.020 --> 04:01.020
Just what I said. Hurry up and eat.

04:01.020 --> 04:02.020
Yeah, I know.

04:02.020 --> 04:06.020
But why hurry up?

04:06.020 --> 04:09.020
You're going bowling tonight, aren't you?

04:09.020 --> 04:10.020
Yes.

04:10.020 --> 04:13.020
I might go bowling tonight.

04:13.020 --> 04:16.020
And then again, I might not go bowling tonight.

04:16.020 --> 04:22.020
Oh, Ralph, you gotta go.

04:22.020 --> 04:24.020
Why do I gotta go?

04:24.020 --> 04:29.020
Well, uh, well, it's the night you generally go, isn't it?

04:29.020 --> 04:30.020
Yeah.

04:30.020 --> 04:33.020
The night I generally go?

04:33.020 --> 04:35.020
You know something, Alex, I've been thinking.

04:35.020 --> 04:39.020
I think I've been leaving you alone too much.

04:39.020 --> 04:41.020
Oh, go on, Ralph.

04:41.020 --> 04:43.020
Every man wants a night out.

04:43.020 --> 04:44.020
Yeah.

04:44.020 --> 04:49.020
And a lot of guys like the afternoon out.

04:49.020 --> 04:51.020
Hey, what's the matter with you tonight?

04:51.020 --> 04:55.020
What you acting so stupid about?

04:55.020 --> 04:56.020
You're right, Alex.

04:56.020 --> 04:58.020
I'm stupid, all right.

04:58.020 --> 04:59.020
I'm stupid.

04:59.020 --> 05:04.020
No one knows any better, not even me, than you, how stupid I am.

05:04.020 --> 05:06.020
What happened to you today?

05:06.020 --> 05:10.020
Did something fall on your head?

05:10.020 --> 05:13.020
Yes, the worst.

05:13.020 --> 05:16.020
All right, Ralph, if you've got something on your mind, come out with it.

05:16.020 --> 05:19.020
All right, I'll come out with it.

05:19.020 --> 05:23.020
There it is.

05:23.020 --> 05:24.020
Well, uh...

05:24.020 --> 05:25.020
Don't well!

05:25.020 --> 05:30.020
Don't well explain it to me.

05:30.020 --> 05:31.020
I...

05:31.020 --> 05:36.020
No, I, I, I, not everyone is going to know.

05:36.020 --> 05:37.020
I can't.

05:37.020 --> 05:38.020
You can't?

05:38.020 --> 05:39.020
You can't explain it?

05:39.020 --> 05:41.020
Then I'll explain it to you.

05:41.020 --> 05:43.020
I'll explain it to you.

05:43.020 --> 05:49.020
You played me for a soap, Alex, for a long time, but I finally caught up with you.

05:49.020 --> 05:51.020
Aren't you ashamed of yourself?

05:51.020 --> 05:53.020
Aren't you ashamed?

05:53.020 --> 05:59.020
Me out working hard all day, and you running around with some sleep, by the name of Joe.

05:59.020 --> 06:01.020
You ought to be ashamed of yourself.

06:01.020 --> 06:02.020
No!

06:02.020 --> 06:03.020
Don't well!

06:03.020 --> 06:06.020
Maybe that Joe has got Cadillacs.

06:06.020 --> 06:11.020
Maybe Joe's got fancy clothes, or maybe Joe's got fingernails that are manicured.

06:11.020 --> 06:16.020
Well, I could have had Cadillacs, and I could have had manicured nails, and I could have had fancy clothes.

06:16.020 --> 06:18.020
But I didn't throw my money away on anything foolish like that.

06:18.020 --> 06:19.020
No, sir.

06:19.020 --> 06:31.020
I took what little money I had and got a twin burial plot for us.

06:31.020 --> 06:35.020
I'm not taking this way and down, Alex.

06:35.020 --> 06:36.020
Now, ask yourself.

06:36.020 --> 06:39.020
I'm going to get over there, and you let him in.

06:39.020 --> 06:40.020
Oh, God, please.

06:40.020 --> 06:44.020
Mrs. Amy, let him in.

06:44.020 --> 06:48.020
Let him in!

06:48.020 --> 06:51.020
All right, now.

06:51.020 --> 06:53.020
Has he gone yet?

06:53.020 --> 06:55.020
I've got the ring.

06:55.020 --> 06:57.020
You got the ring for me, huh?

06:57.020 --> 07:00.020
Well, I got one for you, and I'm going to put it right around your eye!

07:00.020 --> 07:01.020
Just a minute!

07:01.020 --> 07:02.020
Don't give me just a minute!

07:02.020 --> 07:03.020
Get him off!

07:03.020 --> 07:04.020
We're going!

07:04.020 --> 07:05.020
Oh, stop it!

07:05.020 --> 07:06.020
Come on!

07:06.020 --> 07:07.020
Stop it!

07:07.020 --> 07:08.020
Don't tell me to stop!

07:08.020 --> 07:09.020
I'll explain, then.

07:09.020 --> 07:10.020
Go ahead and explain.

07:10.020 --> 07:11.020
This is Joe Benson.

07:11.020 --> 07:12.020
He's a jeweler.

07:12.020 --> 07:17.020
He was nice enough to look all over with me, trying to find you a decent ring I could afford.

07:17.020 --> 07:21.020
I never see you for Christmas, but that's a little silly now.

07:21.020 --> 07:23.020
I'm very sorry, Joe.

07:23.020 --> 07:25.020
I'm sorry I put you on this spot.

07:25.020 --> 07:26.020
Oh, it's all right.

07:26.020 --> 07:28.020
It wasn't anything.

07:28.020 --> 07:30.020
Well, I guess I'll go.

07:30.020 --> 07:48.020
Good night.

07:48.020 --> 08:05.020
Alice, I'm going to go.

08:05.020 --> 08:08.020
I know you don't want me around after that.

08:08.020 --> 08:11.020
I'm sorry.

08:11.020 --> 08:16.020
I hope you'll forgive me.

08:16.020 --> 08:21.020
Well...

08:21.020 --> 08:23.020
Yeah?

08:23.020 --> 08:27.020
I not only forgive you, I thank you.

08:27.020 --> 08:29.020
Thank you?

08:29.020 --> 08:35.020
It might sound a little corny, but not every woman has a husband who's still jealous of her

08:35.020 --> 08:40.020
after 12 years of married life.

08:40.020 --> 08:46.020
Maybe you'd like to break.

